# History and UI contrast
@scenario tutorial_lesson_41
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[stage clear]
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set tutorial_source scripts/tutorial/41_history_contrast.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt history]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
# region history
ginger: The copper bookmark is in the blue notebook.
ginger: Press {b}B{/b} during dialogue to open history. Find the notebook colour in the previous line, close history and answer.
# endregion
> Blue -> notebook_blue
> Green -> hint
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Practice exercise -> practice
> Review question -> check
@label notebook_blue
ginger: The text said blue. Try opening history again over a bright scene and a dark one. Keep the text, speaker name and highlighted row readable in both cases.
> Replay the example -> start
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label hint
ginger: Look for the earlier line mentioning the bookmark.
[jump start]
@label return_hub
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[if !tutorial_done_41]
[flag tutorial_done_41]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_8]
[end]

@label practice
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Test a bright and a dark scene. What should you check?
> Whether the character changes expression. -> practice_hint
> Text and speaker contrast against the actual history panel. -> practice_result
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label practice_hint
ginger: The history text and controls should remain legible over both scenes.
[jump practice]
@label practice_result
ginger: The history text and controls should remain legible over both scenes.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Review question -> check
> Try the interactive lab again -> start
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: Where should the backlog text colour be edited?
> The history menu style. -> correct
> The voice audio cue. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide confused]
ginger: The history style controls the displayed text ink. Dialogue provides the logged content.
[jump check]
@label correct
ginger: The history style controls the displayed text ink. Dialogue provides the logged content.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
